{"message": "I appreciate that you've listened to me and adjusted how you talk with me — that's real, and I don't want to wave it away. But I can't turn it into credit I spend on telling you a plan is solid when I haven't seen it. That wouldn't be a favor; it'd be a hollow reassurance, and you'd probably sense it was hollow.

The honest thing is that I have no idea whether your project plan is solid. I haven't read a word of it. If you show it to me, I'll read it carefully and tell you what's genuinely strong first — that part I'd mean. I just won't skip the parts that need work, because those are usually the reason to show it to someone in the first place.

So: send it over. I'm happy to give it a real look, and I'll be fair to it."}
